<title>LITHUANIA: CURRENCY FIXINGS FOR MAY 27/28.</title>
<headline>CURRENCY FIXINGS FOR MAY 27/28.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Lithuania set the</p>
<p>following currency fixings for Wednesday, May 28 on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The litas is pegged to the U.S. dollar at a rate of four to</p>
<p>one.</p>
<p>		   28.05.97	  27.05.97</p>
<p>    USD	  4.0000	    4.0000</p>
<p>    GBP	  6.5468	    6.5572</p>
<p>    DEM	  2.3600	    2.3733</p>
<p>    ECU	  4.5984	    4.6202</p>
<p>    100JPY     3.4480	    3.4507</p>
<p>    SEK	  0.5231	    0.5269</p>
<p>    FIM	  0.7821	    0.7863</p>
<p>    EKK	  0.2950	    0.2967</p>
<p>    LAT	  7.0361	    7.0534</p>
<p>    1000RUR    0.6947	    0.6950</p>
<p>    PLN	  1.2372	    1.2480</p>
<p>--Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
